= Knowledge domain category =

Shared composition surface for substantive top-level Domain categories.

The template centralizes the stable parts of Domain-category behavior:

* the distinction between category membership and semantic Domain identity;
* a live <code>#ask</code> table over <code>Property:Domain</code>;
* navigation to the corresponding portal-title projection and exemplar;
* optional linkage to a reusable SMW Concept.

Each category remains responsible for its own domain-specific scope, inclusion and exclusion/boundary language. This keeps rendered categories rich without copy-pasting structural boilerplate.

<pre>
{{Knowledge domain category
 |domain=Physics
 |scope=...
 |includes=...
 |boundary=...
 |exemplar=Momentum
 |related=* Related: [[:Category:Mathematics]]
}}
</pre>

Do not use this template for administrative categories or focused subject categories merely for visual consistency.

See [[BITwiki:Templates and categories]] and [[BITwiki:MediaWiki substrate]].

[[Category:BITwiki templates]]
